--- array-map-type-as-function ---
// A type is callable via its constructor, so it works as a mapper function.
#test((1, 2, 3).map(str), ("1", "2", "3"))
#test(("1", "2", "3").map(int), (1, 2, 3))
│ #document[]

--- array-sorted-type-as-key ---
// A type is callable, so it works as a named `key` function (sorting by the
// string representation of each element).
#test((2, 1, 10).sorted(key: str), (1, 10, 2))
│ #document[]
